     "notes": "To wrap up the day, let's look at where cases get stuck, starting with mediation. Think of these as compromise traps. The first is a medical ledger or lien picture that isn't verified. Unreconciled hospital bills or missing final treatment records leave the defense with damages it can't confirm. On our file, Riverton Spine and Rehab's ledger still carries a duplicate visit, so the audited figure of six thousand one hundred five dollars has to stand on the attendance log. The second trap is missing decision-makers. If the adjuster or defense representative in the room lacks full settlement authority, and nothing was pre-negotiated, nobody can say yes. The third is brief misalignment. A brief that arrives late, or without key exhibits like MRIs and crash diagrams, leaves the mediator unprepared. That's why our statement and binder were due to Judge Benton a full week ahead. Notice that the first and third traps are things your own prep can prevent."
